\import{fdip-macros}
\meta{agent-authored}{true}
\tag{fdip}
\taxon{Example}
\title{Equal determinants for two inequivalent character lines}
\date{2026-11-17}

\p{Let a generator of #{C_3} act on #{F=\mathbb C} by
#{\zeta=\ue^{2\pi\ui /3}}. Its
[algebraic dual action](fdip-00UL) is multiplication by
#{\zeta^{-1}}. A nonzero complex-linear intertwiner between
the lines would imply #{\zeta=\zeta^{-1}}, contrary to
#{\zeta^2+\zeta+1=0}. Thus no chosen bilinear self-duality
exists.}

\p{On the one-vertex cellular circle, use the generator as
its link. The inverse-transport formulas of
[the cochain operators](fdip-00SR) give, in degree order #{0,1},
##{K_F=\begin{pmatrix}
 m&\zeta-1\\\zeta^{-1}-1&m
\end{pmatrix},\qquad K_{F^*}=K_F^{\mathsf T}.}
Since #{(\zeta-1)(\zeta^{-1}-1)=3}, both determinants equal
#{m^2-3}. This equality does not supply the missing intertwiner.
The usual invariant Hermitian pairing on the line is
sesquilinear, rather than the bilinear form required by that
self-duality.}
